      "profile": "coefficient",
      "source_problem": "$\\int \\frac{2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "source_solution": "First, let $u=x+1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
